div.h4:
Importance of Preaching the Gospel;
Perverseness of Israel. (a.
d. 58.)

Tenderness in Reproving; Self-Examination;
Spiritual Mindedness and Beneficence. (a.
d. 56.)

div.p:
We now heard what the apostle renounced;
let us now see what he laid hold on, and resolved to cleave to,
namely, Christ and heaven. He had his heart on these two great
peculiarities of the Christian religion.

div.h4:
The Apostle's Directions to Timothy;
Salutations and Benedictions. (a.
d. 66.)

div.p:
Thus far is the preface to the epistle;
then follows the entrance into the matter, by signifying the end of
Titus's being left in Crete.

div.h4:
The Apostle's Plea for Onesimus;
Salutations. (a.
d. 62.)

Origin of War and Contention; Against Pride;
Submission to God. (a.
d. 61.)

Sobriety, Watchfulness, and Charity;
Improvement of Talents. (a.
d. 66.)

div.p:
1. That they should not think them strange,
nor be surprised at them, as if some unexpected event befel them;
for,

div.h4:
Exhortation to the Faithful;
Conclusion. (a.
d. 66.)
